         await pg.close()\",\"+        await b.close()\",\"+asyncio.run(main())\"]}],\"created\":true},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125821__x600c07/agent.4.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":617,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":617,\"newLines\":9,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_progress\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CWTzDCUViAPWKJiorHvoFU-heartbeat-1\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CWTzDCUViAPWKJiorHvoFU\\\",\\\"elapsed_time_seconds\\\":60,\\\"heartbeat\\\":true,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"c223f3ce-c273-45b2-8cb9-6820ae465d31\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"task_notification\\\",\\\"task_id\\\":\\\"bwh14jwec\\\",\\\"run_id\\\":\\\"0mw16j2sy-555b0020\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CWTzDCUViAPWKJiorHvoFU\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"output_file\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125821__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-125821/tests/hub; timeout 55 python3 run.py \\\\\\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave\\\\\\\" | head -1; timeout 55 python3 run.py \\\\\\\"players=2&auto=1&scenario=server\\\\\\\" | head -1; rm -f game.html; cd ../..; cp ../Wiretap*.html /tmp/s55/w.html; timeout 100 python3 tests/smoke.py /tmp/s55/w.html | tail -1\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"5be5b376-40f2-43e3-b796-db36a735ffd5\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CWTzDCUViAPWKJiorHvoFU\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave {\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"fails\\\\\\\":[]}\\\\nplayers=2&auto=1&scenario=server {\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"fails\\\\\\\":[]}\\\\nERRORS 0\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"5533fe4f-d2e0-4b13-9131-ec382932caa7\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T21:09:09.839Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave {\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"fails\\\\\\\":[]}\\\\nplayers=2&auto=1&scenario=server {\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"fails\\\\\\\":[]}\\\\nERRORS 0\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CWTzDCUViAPWKJiorHvoFU\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CgggMggo3YP7HK6DABcgw\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"All four AI Hub harness scenarios now pass on the final bundle, and the final Chromium smoke run reports zero page errors. The two files I checked have the same checksum (`022000a2e064`).\\\\n\\\\nThe same remaining limits as last time stand; I can't close them from this environment:\\\\n- **Real hardware:** There is no real DualSense, TV or iOS Safari. The pad is covered only by a fake gamepad, and WebKit by Playwright's engine.\\\\n- **Visual coverage:** I've viewed the main screens and modes by eye, but not every state of every screen.\\\\n- **Map size:** The map is 48×34, not the plan's 72×56. TASK.md gives no map size and wins where it disagrees with the plan.\\\\n- **Two-player input:** Local two-player is keyboard-only.\\\\n\\\\nThe game is `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-125821.html` in `work/`. `exit-interview.json` sits beside it, parses, and has every field filled.\\\\n\\\\n## Source Information\\\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 13:50\\\\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008)\\\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management shift and a versus mode. Isometric 2.5D with HTML case-file screens.\\\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio.\\\\n- **Art Direction:** Engine-native retro-modern pixel art pushed toward grit.\\\\n- **Animation:** Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs.\\\\n- **Audio:** Code-written chip-synth music, synthesized effects, formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter.\\\\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world, 1–4 players, verified in the harness on the final build. Local split-screen versus for 2 humans on one keyboard. No other network.\\\\n- **Testing:** Playwright (Chromium and WebKit) smoke runs, a scripted chase, a fake DualSense, touch-only emulation, all missions under the attract bot, a two-player split-screen run, and the AI Hub harness in four scenarios, all passing on the final build. Not tested: real iOS Safari, a real controller, a real TV, or a visual review of every scene.\\\\n- **Research:** The engine docs, the AI Hub client and README, and PLAN.md. Knowledge of the series from memory.\\\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\\\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\\\\n- **Usage:** unknown.\\\\n\\\\n## Testing Feedback\\\\n- **Issues caught:** About 10. They were the menu staying open over missions and attract, tail state leaking between missions, a tail succeeding with no contact, a fake pad injected too late, overlapping toasts, a broken Person constructor in my first draft, two hub-harness failures, and the mission HUD showing behind modal screens.\\\\n- **Critical:** None known remain. The menu over missions and the briefing blocking hub traffic were the serious ones.\\\\n- **Most helpful test:** The AI Hub harness, which found two real multiplayer bugs. Running every mission under the attract bot was second.\\\\n- **Least helpful test:** Node syntax checks, which passed while the game was still wrong at runtime.\\\\n\\\\n## Engine Feedback\\\\n- **Liked most:** Everything is drawn by code and still looks good: shaded rigs, lighting, rain, the ready-made pause and settings screens, and built-in split screen.\\\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I guessed at the mouse-ground return shape and at how settings groups show up. Running it in a browser settled both.\\\\n- **Built myself:** The investigation screens as a small DOM kit, the \\\\\\\"made\\\\\\\" perception loop, and the hub netcode.\\\\n- **Hardest part:** Knowing which parts of a very large API to trust without seeing them.\\\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** Nothing needs removing. I'd merge Dialog and Shell into one text path.\\\\n- **Change one thing:** A built-in right-stick aim helper that applies the player's axis inversion.\\\\n\\\\n## Prompt Feedback\\\\n- **Liked most:** The plan's concrete data, the controller-first rules and the explicit deliverables list.\\\\n- **Confusing:** The plan describes more than a medium-effort build covers (a 72×56 map), so I built to TASK.md with a smaller 48×34 map.\\\\n- **Hardest:** Keeping the demo complete while honoring the 10-foot rules without a real pad or TV.\\\\n- **One test I'd run:** A real DualSense in a browser.\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":573,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":299005,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":573},\\\"output_tokens\\\":781,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"6addb4d6-aeaa-4174-9905-6d53413571f7\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T21:09:18.009Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CgggMgPwLUaauFVty8Vym\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Stop hook feedback:\\\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections exist, but TASK.md requires every feature to be implemented and verified, and the transcript does not establish that. The final reply admits the map is 48×34 rather than the plan's 72×56, that local two-player is keyboard-only, that not every state of every screen was visually reviewed, and that real controller, TV and iOS Safari testing were not done. Those gaps keep the 'feature-complete demo with all features shown working' requirement from being established.\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"f78bb234-a97c-4e66-b0f6-eb757cc0ed8e\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T21:09:22.436Z\\\",\\\"isSynthetic\\\":true}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5584c513-9280-4b46-aaca-c597f867a104\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"28ef2795-1700-4f42-8e3e-233760312f12\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":150,\\\"estimated_tok