llowed by the flow test that drove beats to completion; together they found the name collisions and proved there were no softlocks.\\\",\\n  \\\"The first version of the headless beat test, which compared game.errors counts; the engine logs a repeated error once, so it reported passes while missions were failing.\\\"],\\n \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n  \\\"How much comes for free and works the same headless: the standard pause/settings/controls/saves, E.Shell's HUD, E.Suspicion, sight cones, flow fields and a fixed-step clock that made deterministic Node tests easy.\\\",\\n  \\\"Yes: I assumed shape materials accepted names like 'rusted' and 'linen' as patterns (they are materials, not patterns), and I first missed that pointer events don't report a second mouse button, so left-click while holding right never reached the input.\\\",\\n  \\\"The wire room (call scheduler, minimization windows, spot-checks, logging key lines in time, voice ID) and the DOM UI kit with spatial focus navigation, hover focus and device-following glyph legends.\\\",\\n  \\\"Knowing what exists in a very large API: the index is huge, so finding the right call (toCell's return shape, mouseGround, input.held) took grepping and small experiments.\\\",\\n  \\\"The error reporting that dedupes repeated errors: it hides how often something fails, which misled my first tests; I would overhaul it to keep a count per message.\\\",\\n  \\\"Built-in chorded mouse button support (and a documented way to read raw gamepad axes for a second stick), so watch-and-shoot schemes work with a mouse out of the box.\\\"],\\n \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n  \\\"It asks for a complete vertical slice with real infrastructure (attract mode, AI Hub, controller-first UX, an About screen) rather than a toy, and the plan it came with was specific enough to build from.\\\",\\n  \\\"The plan targeted a 60-75 minute five-episode game with a different file name and model; at medium effort scoping that down while keeping every system was a judgment call the prompt leaves open.\\\",\\n  \\\"Fitting every system (field surveillance, chase, tail, box, cipher, affidavit and judge, wire room, the corner as Tee, versus with networking, attract) into one coherent, working build in a single session.\\\",\\n  \\\"A real human playthrough of the full story on a TV with a DualSense, start to credits, to judge pacing and readability at 10 feet.\\\"],\\n \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"WIRETAP\\\",\\n  \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Somebody's always listening.\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Wire (2002-2008)\\\",\\n  \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n  \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick/WASD move · L2/right mouse watch · R2/left click photo · Cross/E interact · Triangle/Q partner, orders, call out · Create/Tab notebook\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"story\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"isometric\\\", \\\"crime\\\", \\\"stealth\\\"]}}\\njson.dump(c, open(p,'w'), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)\\nEOF\\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && python3 -c \\\"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']),all(d['sourceInformation'].values()))\\\" && grep -c \\\"TODO\\\\|FIXME\\\\|placeholder\\\" src/*.js | grep -v \\\":0\\\"; node tests/headless.mjs 2>&1 | tail -2; node tests/rules.mjs | tail -1; ls -la ..\",\"description\":\"Write the exit interview, rebuild, verify JSON and rerun tests\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3797,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":543595,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3797},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"90c0e12f-02cb-4f48-b07b-9e01e40f5f84\",\"uuid\":\"9fbc2977-640c-47b7-90fe-fafa6bc090a5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T21:14:06.443Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgggh6N6yVKpz78ibTf17\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01N89MDTu11P1pimrxzQMKJ8\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125818__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-125818 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\np='src/credits.json'; c=json.load(open(p))\\nc['exitInterview'] = {\\n \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-03 12:58\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Wire (2002-2008)\\\",\\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth investigation / crime drama, with a corner-management sim (playing the crew) and an asymmetric hidden-identity versus mode\\\",\\n  \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric 2.5D over a 72x56-cell West Baltimore neighborhood (camera turns in 90-degree steps); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens for the Board, notebook, wire room, box and affidavit\\\",\\n  \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D lighting, E.Shell HTML HUD, E.Dialog, E.Suspicion, FlowField, shapes as data); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript in one IIFE; Web Audio; bundled by a Node script into one HTML file\\\",\\n  \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlights, rain, Formstone and brick rowhouses, boarded vacants, phone wires with sneakers over the corner, neon store signs; case-file manila, corkboard and phosphor-green wire-room UI\\\",\\n  \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (walk/run/crouch, engine poses for sitting, phoning, camera-raise, hands up, cuffed), live portraits in dialogue and polaroids, tweens and timers; no frame lists\\\",\\n  \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-written chip music in the engine's song format with layered tension (8 songs), synthesized effects (shutter, pager, DTMF tones, sirens, cuffs, fence rattles), filtered-noise ambience beds, and Animalese-style gibberish voices from formant grains synced to typed text, with a telephone filter on the wire\\\",\\n  \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative sim, 10 Hz snapshots under 1,100 bytes, client-reported movement with host speed checks, validated actions, leave-to-bot, server host, finish with standings/scores/stats/awards); local split-screen versus for 2; no other network use\\\",\\n  \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Lightweight, token-efficient: headless Node vm tests (boot, every story beat, attract reel loops, a bots-only 5-minute versus round, corner ledger, cipher, photo scoring, perception targets, box thresholds, affidavit scoring, montage on every branch, flow tests driving the cold open, chase, box, wire shift, Tee's night, paper/judge, raid and long lens to completion); Playwright Chromium screenshots of title and key screens, mouse photo, fake DualSense glyphs/Xbox setting/stick inversion; WebKit iPhone touch-only notice and attract; AI Hub harness all four runs passed; viewport-matrix spot check (2 phones, 5 desktop sizes, all clean). Real iOS Safari not tested.\\\",\\n  \\\"research\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, parts of AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, the stealth kit and template) and the AI Hub protocol README; the provided PLAN.md; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\\\",\\n  \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\",\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\\n  \\\"usage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\\n \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n  \\\"About 15 issues: an h() helper that dropped array children (the title menu and most screens rendered empty), the flags accessor F() colliding with missions' F parameter, Versus.view colliding with the scene's view setting, FD missing its interact method, corner runners stuck on a goal inside a wall, double-charging customers after a shutdown, chorded left-click while holding right mouse never registering (no photos with a mouse), touch-only detection failing in WebKit, a syntax error in the cipher screen, walking-past perception too strict, Annex cast standing inside desks, stacked screens showing through each other, the About deep link opening over the menu, the attract box vignette exiting attract by tapping input, and interlude targets set too high.\\\",\\n  \\\"Seven were game-breaking: the empty screens, the F() collision, the Versus.view collision, the missing interact, the stuck sale cycle, the chorded mouse click and the cipher syntax error.\\\",\\n  \\\"The headless pass that started every story beat and counted console errors, followed by the flow test that drove beats to completion; together they found the name collisions and proved there were no softlocks.\\\",\\n  \\\"The first version of the headless beat test, which compared game.errors counts; the engine logs a repeated error once, so it reported passes while missions were failing.\\\"],\\n \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n  \\\"How much comes for free and works the same headless: the standard pause/settings/controls/saves, E.Shell's HUD, E.Suspicion, sight cones, flow fields and a fixed-step clock that made deterministic Node tests easy.\\\",\\n  \\\"Yes: I assumed shape materials accepted names like 'rusted' and 'linen' as patterns (they are materials, not patterns), and I first missed that pointer events don't report a second mouse button, so left-click while holding right never reached the input.\\\",\\n  \\\"The wire room (call scheduler, minimization windows, spot-checks, logging key lines in time, voice ID) and the DOM UI kit with spatial focus navigation, hover focus and device-following glyph legends.\\\",\\n  \\\"Knowing what exists in a very large API: the index is huge, so finding the right call (toCell's return shape, mouseGround, input.held) took grepping and small experiments.\\\",\\n  \\\"The error reporting that dedupes repeated errors: it hides how often something fails, which misled my first tests; I would overhaul it to keep a count per message.\\\",\\n  \\\"Built-in chorded mouse button support (and a documented way to read raw gamepad axes for a second stick), so watch-and-shoot schemes work with a mouse out of the box.\\\"],\\n \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n  \\\"It asks for a complete vertical slice with real infrastructure (attract mode, AI Hub, controller-first UX, an About screen) rather than a toy, and the plan it came with was specific enough to build from.\\\",\\n  \\\"The plan targeted a 60-75 minute five-episode game with a different file name and model; at medium effort scoping that down while keeping every system was a judgment call the prompt leaves open.\\\",\\n  \\\"Fitting every system (field surveillance, chase, tail, box, cipher, affidavit and judge, wire room, the corner as Tee, versus with networking, attract) into one coherent, working build in a single session.\\\",\\n  \\\"A real human playthrough of the full story on a TV with a DualSense, start to credits, to judge pacing and readability at 10 feet.\\\"],\\n \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"WIRETAP\\\",\\n  \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Somebody's always listening.\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Wire (2002-2008)\\\",\\n  \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n  \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick/WASD move · L2/right mouse watch · R2/left click photo · Cross/E interact · Triangle/Q partner, orders, call out · Create/Tab notebook\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"story\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"isometric\\\", \\\"crime\\\", \\\"stealth\\\"]}}\\njson.dump(c, open(p,'w'), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)\\nEOF\\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && python3 -c \\\"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']),all(d['sourceInformation'].values()))\\\" && grep -c \\\"TODO\\\\|FIXME\\\\|placeholder\\\" src/*.js | grep -v \\\":0\\\"; node tests/headless.mjs 2>&1 | tail -2; node tests/rules.mjs | tail -1; ls -la ..\",\"description\":\"Write the exit interview, rebuild, verify JSON and rerun tests\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01N89MDTu11P1pimrxzQMKJ8\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125818__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-125818\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\",\"task_id\":\"bm0gfes25\",\"run_id\":\"0mw16r0zr-da8c7c89\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01N89MDTu11P1pimrxzQMKJ8\",\"description\":\"Write the exit interview, rebuild, verify JSON and rerun tests\",\"is_backgrounded\":false,\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"uuid\":\"a74739a3-ac71-489f-a8c3-5a6c68d46a0c\",\"session_id\":\"90c0e12f-02cb-4f48-b07b-9e01e40f5f84\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_notification\",\"task_id\":\"bm0gfes25\",\"run_id\":\"0mw16r0zr-da8c7c89\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01N89MDTu11P1pimrxzQMKJ8\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"output_file\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Write the exit interview, rebuild, verify JSON and rerun tests\",\"uuid\":\"977a68eb-c27e-43d9-9f25-6df3cfadd4fa\",\"session_id\":\"90c0e12f-02cb-4f48-b07b-9e01e40f5f84\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125818__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-125818.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":15328,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15328,"newLines":7,"lines":[" })(typeof My3D2dge !== 'undefined' ? My3D2dge : undefined);"," </script>"," <script>(() => { 'use strict';","-const CREDITS = {\"credits\":[\"WIRETAP\",\"An original game inspired by The Wire (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\",\"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max effort); built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort).\",\"Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT).\",\"Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\",\"All art, music, sound and voices are generated by code. No asset files.\"],\"roll\":[\"WIRETAP\",\"Somebody's always listening.\",\"\",\"\",\"DESIGN AND CODE\",\"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\",\"\",\"\",\"ENGINE\",\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 · Michael Crosato\",\"\",\"\",\"ONLINE\",\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1\",\"\",\"\",\"CAST\",\"Det. Dana Whitlock · Det. Lou Szabo\",\"Det. Hal Pettiford · Officer Ren Ocasio\",\"Lt. Gil Navarre · Maj. Leland Pruitt\",\"Terrence 'Tee' Mabry · Ricky 'Rook' Batts\",\"Corey Lyle · Junior 'Pigeon' Hollis\",\"Darnell 'Easy' Booker · Lonnie Fitch\",\"Miss Odessa Tillman · Wesley 'Pockets' Gaines\",\"\",\"INSPIRED BY\",\"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\"\",\"\",\"TO BE CONTINUED\"],\"questions\":{\"testing\":[\"How many issues did testing catch?\",\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\",\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\",\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"],\"engine\":[\"What did you like most about the engine?\",\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\",\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\",\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\",\"If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from engine, what would that be?\",\"If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\"],\"prompt\":[\"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\"What was confusing?\",\"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\"If there was one test you could of run, what would that test be?\"]},\"exitInterview\":{\"sourceInformation\":{},\"testingFeedback\":[],\"engineFeedback\":[],\"promptFeedback\":[],\"aiHub\":{}}};","+const CREDITS = {\"credits\":[\"WIRETAP\",\"An original game inspired by The Wire (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\",\"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max effort); built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort).\",\"Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT).\",\"Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\",\"All art, music, sound and voices are generated by code. No asset files.\"],\"roll\":[\"WIRETAP\",\"Somebody's always listening.\",\"\",\"\",\"DESIGN AND CODE\",\"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\",\"\",\"\",\"ENGINE\",\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 · Michael Crosato\",\"\",\"\",\"ONLINE\",\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1\",\"\",\"\",\"CAST\",\"Det. Dana Whitlock · Det. Lou Szabo\",\"Det. Hal Pettiford · Officer Ren Ocasio\",\"Lt. Gil Navarre · Maj. Leland Pruitt\",\"Terrence 'Tee' Mabry · Ricky 'Rook' Batts\",\"Corey Lyle · Junior 'Pigeon' Hollis\",\"Darnell 'Easy' Booker · Lonnie Fitch\",\"Miss Odessa Tillman · Wesley 'Pockets' Gaines\",\"\",\"INSPIRED BY\",\"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\"\",\"\",\"TO BE CONTINUED\"],\"questions\":{\"testing\":[\"How many issues did testing catch?\",\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\",\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\",\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"],\"engine\":[\"What did you like most about the engine?\",\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\",\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\",\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\",\"If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from engine, what would that be?\",\"If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\"],\"prompt\":[\"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\"What was confusing?\",\"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\"If there was one test you could of run, what would that test be?\"]},\"exitInterview\":{\"sourceInformation\":{\"date\":\"2026-11-03 12:58\",\"source\":\"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\"genre\":\"Stealth investigation / crime drama, with a corner-management sim (playing the crew) and an asymmetric hidden-identity versus mode\",\"perspective\":\"Isometric 2.5D over a 72x56-cell West Baltimore neighborhood (camera turns in 90-degree steps); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens for the Board, notebook, wire room, box and affidavit\",\"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D lighting, E.Shell HTML HUD, E.Dialog, E.Suspicion, FlowField, shapes as data); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript in one IIFE; Web Audio; bundled by a Node script into one HTML file\",\"artDirection\":\"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlights, rain, Formstone and brick rowhouses, boarded vacants, phone wires with sneakers over the corner, neon store signs; case-file manila, corkboard and phosphor-green wire-room UI\",\"animation\":\"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (walk/run/crouch, engine poses for sitting, phoning, camera-raise, hands up, cuffed), live portraits in dialogue and polaroids, tweens and timers; no frame lists\",\"audio\":\"Code-written chip music in the engine's song format with layered tension (8 songs), synthesized effects (shutter, pager, DTMF tones, sirens, cuffs, fence rattles), filtered-noise ambience beds, and Animalese-style gibberish voices from formant grains synced to typed text, with a telephone filter on the wire\",\"online\":\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative sim, 10 Hz snapshots under 1,100 bytes, client-reported movement with host speed checks, validated actions, leave-to-bot, server host, finish with standings/scores/stats/awards); local split-screen versus for 2; no other network use\",\"testing\":\"Lightweight, token-efficient: headless Node vm tests (boot, every story beat, attract reel loops, a bots-only 5-minute versus round, corner ledger, cipher, photo scoring, perception targets, box thresholds, affidavit scoring, montage on every branch, flow tests driving the cold open, chase, box, wire shift, Tee's night, paper/judge, raid and long lens to completion); Playwright Chromium screenshots of title and key screens, mouse photo, fake DualSense glyphs/Xbox setting/stick inversion; WebKit iPhone touch-only notice and attract; AI Hub harness all four runs passed; viewport-matrix spot check (2 phones, 5 desktop sizes, all clean). Real iOS Safari not tested.\",\"research\":\"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, parts of AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, the stealth kit and template) and the AI Hub protocol README; the provided PLAN.md; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\",\"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\"usage\":\"unknown\"},\"testingFeedback\":[\"About 15 issues: an h() helper that dropped array children (the title menu and most screens rendered empty), the flags accessor F() colliding with missions' F parameter, Versus.view colliding with the scene's view setting, FD missing its interact method, corner runners stuck on a goal inside a wall, double-charging customers after a shutdown, chorded left-click while holding right mouse never registering (no photos with a mouse), touch-only detection failing in WebKit, a syntax error in the cipher screen, walking-past perception too strict, Annex cast standing inside desks, stacked screens showing through each other, the About deep link opening over the menu, the attract box vignette exiting attract by tapping input, and interlude targets set too high.\",\"Seven were game-breaking: the empty screens, the F() collision, the Versus.view collision, the missing interact, the stuck sale cycle, the chorded mouse click and the cipher syntax error.\",\"The headless pass that started every story beat and counted console errors, followed by the flow test that drove beats to completion; together they found the name collisions and proved there were no softlocks.\",\"The first version of the headless beat test, which compared game.errors counts; the engine logs a repeated error once, so it reported passes while missions were failing.\"],\"engineFeedback\":[\"How much comes for free and works the same headless: the standard pause/settings/controls/saves, E.Shell's HUD, E.Suspicion, sight cones, flow fields and a fixed-step clock that made deterministic Node tests easy.\",\"Yes: I assumed shape materials accepted names like 'rusted' and 'linen' as patterns (they are materials, not patterns), and I first missed that pointer events don't report a second mouse button, so left-click while holding right never reached the input.\",\"The wire room (call scheduler, minimization windows, spot-checks, logging key lines in time, voice ID) and the DOM UI kit with spatial focus navigation, hover focus and device-following glyph legends.\",\"Knowing what exists in a very large API: the index is huge, so finding the right call (toCell's return shape, mouseGround, input.held) took grepping and small experiments.\",\"The error reporting that dedupes repeated errors: it hides how often something fails, which misled my first tests; I would overhaul it to keep a count per message.\",\"Built-in chorded mouse button support (and a documented way to read raw gamepad axes for a second stick), so watch-and-shoot schemes work with a mouse out of the box.\"],\"promptFeedback\":[\"It asks for a complete vertical slice with real infrastructure (attract mode, AI Hub, controller-first UX, an About screen) rather than a toy, and the plan it came with was specific enough to build from.\",\"The plan targeted a 60-75 minute five-episode game with a different file name and model; at medium effort scoping that down while keeping every system was a judgment call the prompt leaves open.\",\"Fitting every system (field surveillance, chase, tail, box, cipher, affidavit and judge, wire room, the corner as Tee, versus with networking, attract) into one coherent, working build in a single session.\",\"A real human playthrough of the full story on a TV with a DualSense, start to credits, to judge pacing and readability at 10 feet.\"],\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"WIRETAP\",\"tagline\":\"Somebody's always listening.\",\"description\":\"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Stealth\",\"source\":\"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\"series\":\"\",\"players\":\"1–4\",\"controls\":\"Stick/WASD move · L2/right mouse watch · R2/left click photo · Cross/E interact · Triangle/Q partner, orders, call out · Create/Tab notebook\",\"tags\":[\"story\",\"versus\",\"pixel art\",\"isometric\",\"crime\",\"stealth\"]}}};"," /* ---- 00-core.js ---- */"," // WIRETAP: core. The engine alias, constants, registries, the event bus, seeded randomness and the one save STATE."," const E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp } = E;"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-125818__x600c07/work/Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-125818/dev-bundle.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":5,"lines":[" (() => { 'use strict';","-const CREDITS = {\"credits\":[\"WIRETAP\",\"An original game inspired by The Wire (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\",\"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max effort); built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort).\",\"Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT).\",\"Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\",\"All art, music, sound and voices are generated by code. No asset files.\"],\"roll\":[\"W