{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgggtYQ67iGtCrFk9kf85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the build again against the three gaps the stop hook raised. Nothing is stubbed, and every TASK.md feature is in the shipped file.\n\n**No TODOs, placeholders or stubs.** I searched the game source, the credits file and `exit-interview.json` for TODO, FIXME, XXX, stub, placeholder, lorem, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\" and TBD. Nothing came up. Every field in the exit interview has a value. The only one left empty is the AI Hub `series` field, which the schema allows to be empty, so I left it blank on purpose. The test suites still pass: 44 of 44 headless checks, plus the rules and flow tests with no failures.\n\n**Each TASK.md feature is in the bundled html:**\n\n| TASK.md feature | Where it is and how it was checked |\n|---|---|\n| Single html, title from a random draw | `<title>WIRETAP</title>`; WIRETAP came from the plan's random draw |\n| Attract mode | starts after 10 s idle on the title and its menus; any input exits. Checked headless and in WebKit on a touch phone |\n| Multiplayer through AI Hub, and on its own | hub tags, connect, ready and finish; all four harness runs passed. On its own: split-screen versus and bots |\n| Controller-first, keyboard and mouse native | hover focuses, click selects, the mouse aims and takes photos; checked in Playwright |\n| Prompts follow the last device, Xbox option | showed ✕ with a fake DualSense and A after switching to Xbox |\n| Toggles to invert the stick axes | Invert stick left/right and up/down; the left-right one flipped movement in the fake-pad test (+27 → −26) |\n| Touch-only devices | \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button; the demo still runs there |\n| No dense data screens | at most 8 cards per page, large type |\n| About/Credits screen with the four sections | in-game, same text as the exit interview |\n| Exit interview | parses as JSON; 4, 6 and 4 feedback answers, all source fields filled |\n\n**On the other points the hook raised:**\n- \"Usage: unknown\" is what TASK.md asks for when you can't confirm a figure, and I don't have token or cost numbers for this session.\n- Where I differ from PLAN.md, it's because I shortened content, not because a system is missing. Every planned system runs, and the flow tests drive them to the end. STAGE.md says TASK.md wins when the two disagree, and TASK.md asks for a demo long enough to show every feature, not the plan's full 60–75 minutes.\n- The \"60–75 minute\" figure in my prompt feedback is quoted from PLAN.md, not a guess.\n- The lack of a full human playthrough with a controller is a gap in testing. No feature is missing because of it.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 12:58\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** stealth investigation and crime drama, with a sim of running the corner and a cops-vs-corner versus mode. Isometric 2.5D view that turns in 90° steps, side-on interiors, and HTML case-file screens.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript and Web Audio, bundled into one file by a Node script.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's own pixel style made gritty: sodium streetlights, rain, Formstone rowhouses, boarded-up vacants, phone wires with sneakers hanging over the corner.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rigs and poses, live portraits, tweens.\n- **Audio:** 8 layered songs written in code, synthesized sound effects and ambience, and gibberish voices synced to the text, with a phone filter on the wire.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, a shared world for 1–4 players with the host's copy running the game; local split screen; no other network use.\n- **Testing:** headless Node tests (every beat, attract, a versus round, the rules, the flows), Playwright in Chromium and WebKit (mouse, fake gamepad, touch-only), all four AI Hub harness runs, and a viewport sweep on 7 screen sizes. Not tested on real iOS Safari.\n- **Research:** the engine's handoff docs, the AI Hub README, and PLAN.md. The show from memory, no web research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 15.\n2. **How many were critical?** Seven: empty screens, two name collisions, a missing interact function, the corner's sales getting stuck, left-click not registering while the right button is held, and a syntax error.\n3. **Most helpful test:** starting every story beat while counting console errors, then flow tests that play beats through to the end.\n4. **Least helpful test:** my first beat test. It compared the engine's error list, which records a repeated error only once, so it missed failures.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** the standard menus, saves, HUD, perception and pathfinding come built in, and the fixed-step clock makes headless tests easy.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I used material names where the engine wanted pattern names, and I didn't expect the browser to skip the second button press when two mouse buttons are held together.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the wire room, and a menu kit with focus navigation and on-screen prompts that change with the device.\n4. **Hardest part:** finding the right call in a very large API.\n5. **Remove or overhaul:** the error log that hides repeated errors.\n6. **Change one thing:** built-in support for holding two mouse buttons at once.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** it asks for a real vertical slice with all the infrastructure, and the plan is specific.\n2. **Confusing:** the plan describes a 60–75 minute game named for a different model and effort level, so how far to cut it down was left to judgment.\n3. **Hardest:** fitting every system into one working build in a single session.\n4. **One test I'd run:** a full human playthrough with a DualSense on a TV at 10 feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250,"cache_read_input_tokens":555741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":250},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90c0e12f-02cb-4f48-b07b-9e01e40f5f84","uuid":"37acaaf3-7037-4d88-8f7d-d38c7c297dc9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:16:30.386Z","request_id":"req_011CgggtY6j79kuxbGS2HUVD"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled html and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has the four sections, but 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' is not established. The transcript shows the build shortened the planned content (compressed episodes, shortened ops choices, a changed versus seat), and the final reply itself says the demo is 'not the plan's full 60–75 minutes'. It also shows no human playthrough with a controller, which the reply admits is a testing gap. Several features were verified only by headless tests or fake-gamepad automation, not in real play. The condition's 'no stubs' check rests on a grep for marker words, which the transcript shows found nothing, but a grep does not prove features are complete. Because the 'every feature implemented' requirement is not clearly met, the condition is not satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90c0e12f-02cb-4f48-b07b-9e01e40f5f84","uuid":"281b92fd-2f39-45cb-9cfd-bec02049d94b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:16:33.134Z","isSynthetic":true}
